# Per-user topic ACL template for the Mosquitto broker.
# Source: mosquitto.org/documentation/plugins/acl-file/
#
# Default-deny: an authenticated user with no matching "user" block below
# gets NO access at all. A bare "topic" line outside a "user" block would
# apply only to anonymous clients, and allow_anonymous is false in
# deploy/mosquitto.conf, so no such line is written here.
#
# This file is a template. deploy/render-mosquitto-acl.sh replaces @SITE_ID@
# with CMK_SITE_ID at mosquitto container start and writes the result to
# /mosquitto/config/mosquitto.acl. Mosquitto ACL files have no environment
# expansion and `pattern` only knows %u/%c (mosquitto.org/man/mosquitto-conf-5.html),
# so rendering is the way to scope grants to one site subtree. One site per
# deployment; per-site users are a later concern for a shared cloud broker.

user poller
topic readwrite sites/@SITE_ID@/#
# TEMPORARY: lets the poller tombstone pre-namespace retained topics. An
# unauthorized publish is silently dropped by Mosquitto, so narrowing these
# early would orphan the legacy retained data.
# TODO: remove `lan/#` and `admin/#` once every deployment has run a poller
# that sweeps the legacy namespace once.
topic readwrite lan/#
topic readwrite admin/#

user wsreader
topic read sites/@SITE_ID@/lan/#

# Admin dashboard login (`?admin=1`). Its only write grant is the admin command
# topic. Admin topics sit outside `sites/<id>/lan/`, so wsreader never sees
# them. `read sites/<id>/lan/#` is granted so the admin page can show the normal
# dashboard on one connection (user-confirmed 2026-10-02); wsadmin still cannot
# write anywhere under `lan/`.
user wsadmin
topic read sites/@SITE_ID@/lan/#
topic read sites/@SITE_ID@/admin/ack
topic read sites/@SITE_ID@/admin/faked
topic write sites/@SITE_ID@/admin/cmd
